{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "def is_not_prime(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given integer is a non-prime number.\n    Returns True if the number is non-prime, False otherwise (i.e., prime).\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return True  # Numbers less than or equal to 1 are not prime, hence non-prime\n    if number == 2:\n        return False # 2 is prime\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return True  # Even numbers greater than 2 are non-prime\n\n    # Check for odd divisors starting from 3 up to the square root of the number\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= number:\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return True  # Found a divisor, so it's non-prime\n        i += 2\n    return False # No divisors found, so it's prime"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(input_string: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a given character from the string.\n    Returns a new string with the specified character removed from its first and last positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_index = input_string.find(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_index == -1:\n        return input_string\n\n    last_index = input_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_index == last_index:\n        return input_string[:first_index] + input_string[first_index+1:]\n    else:\n        temp_string = input_string[:first_index] + input_string[first_index+1:]\n        last_index_adjusted = temp_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n        return temp_string[:last_index_adjusted] + temp_string[last_index_adjusted+1:]"}
