{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "def sort_matrix(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a matrix (list of lists) by the sum of its rows in ascending order.\n    Uses a helper function to calculate row sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _calculate_row_sum(row):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all numerical elements in a given row.\"\"\"\n        return sum(row)\n\n    # Pair each row with its sum\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        rows_with_sums.append((_calculate_row_sum(row), row))\n\n    # Sort the pairs based on the row sums (the first element of the tuple)\n    sorted_rows_with_sums = sorted(rows_with_sums, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract the original rows from the sorted pairs\n    sorted_matrix = [row for sum_val, row in sorted_rows_with_sums]\n\n    return sorted_matrix"}
