{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "class NumberReverser:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the digits of the input number.\n    Handles positive integers by converting to string, reversing, and converting back.\n    \"\"\"\n    def reverse(self, num: int) -> int:\n        if num < 0:\n            return self.reverse(abs(num))\n\n        s_num = str(num)\n        reversed_s_num = s_num[::-1]\n        return int(reversed_s_num)\n\nclass ConditionEvaluator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    \"\"\"\n    def evaluate(self, num: int, reverser: 'NumberReverser') -> bool:\n        reversed_num = reverser.reverse(num)\n        calculated_value = (2 * reversed_num) - 1\n        return num == calculated_value\n\ndef check(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    This is the main entry point as specified by the SRS.\n    \"\"\"\n    reverser = NumberReverser()\n    evaluator = ConditionEvaluator()\n    return evaluator.evaluate(num, reverser)"}
