{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is undulating.\n    An undulating number has no adjacent digits that are the same, and alternating digits are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_str = str(number)\n    length = len(num_str)\n\n    if length < 2:\n        return True\n\n    for i in range(length - 1):\n        if num_str[i] == num_str[i+1]:\n            return False\n\n    for i in range(length - 2):\n        if num_str[i] != num_str[i+2]:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "def index_minimum(data: list[tuple]) -> object:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value from a list of tuples.\n    Assumes valid input list structure as per design context, including numeric second values.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_second_value = float('inf')\n    result_first_value = None\n\n    for item in data:\n        current_first_value = item[0]\n        current_second_value = item[1]\n\n        if current_second_value < min_second_value:\n            min_second_value = current_second_value\n            result_first_value = current_first_value\n            \n    return result_first_value"}
