{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "class BinaryString:\n    \"\"\"Manages a binary string's value and provides methods for rotation and decimal conversion.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, binary_string: str):\n        self._value = binary_string\n\n    def rotate(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Rotates the binary string by one position to the left.\"\"\"\n        if self._value:\n            self._value = self._value[1:] + self._value[0]\n\n    def to_decimal(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts the current binary string to its decimal integer equivalent.\"\"\"\n        return int(self._value, 2)\n\n    def get_value(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Returns the current binary string value.\"\"\"\n        return self._value\n\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the count of odd decimal equivalents from rotated binary strings up to a specified number of rotations.\"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    binary_str_obj = BinaryString(binary_string)\n\n    for i in range(num_rotations):\n        decimal_value = binary_str_obj.to_decimal()\n        if decimal_value % 2 != 0:\n            odd_count += 1\n        \n        # Rotate for the next iteration, if it's not the last one\n        if i < num_rotations - 1:\n            binary_str_obj.rotate()\n\n    return odd_count"}
