{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable elements in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with the sorted elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    working_list = list(input_list) # Create a copy to ensure a new list is returned.\n    n = len(working_list)\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find index of the maximum element in arr[0...curr_size-1].\n        max_val = working_list[0]\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, curr_size):\n            if working_list[i] > max_val:\n                max_val = working_list[i]\n                max_idx = i\n\n        # Move the maximum element to its correct sorted position.\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            working_list[:max_idx+1] = working_list[:max_idx+1][::-1] # Flip elements to bring max to front.\n            working_list[:curr_size] = working_list[:curr_size][::-1] # Flip elements to move max to end of current sublist.\n\n    return working_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/161", "solution": "def remove_elements(primary_list: list, secondary_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes all elements from primary_list that are also present in secondary_list,\n    preserving the order of remaining elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    secondary_set = set(secondary_list)\n    result_list = []\n    for element in primary_list:\n        if element not in secondary_set:\n            result_list.append(element)\n    return result_list"}
