{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # LIS_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[i]\n    LIS_sum = list(arr)\n    # LDS_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at arr[i]\n    LDS_sum = list(arr)\n\n    # Compute LIS_sum array\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j] and LIS_sum[i] < LIS_sum[j] + arr[i]:\n                LIS_sum[i] = LIS_sum[j] + arr[i]\n\n    # Compute LDS_sum array\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j] and LDS_sum[i] < LDS_sum[j] + arr[i]:\n                LDS_sum[i] = LDS_sum[j] + arr[i]\n\n    # Find the maximum sum of (LIS_sum[i] + LDS_sum[i] - arr[i]) for all i\n    # arr[i] is subtracted to avoid double-counting the peak element\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, LIS_sum[i] + LDS_sum[i] - arr[i])\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
