{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(\n    tuple_collection_1: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...],\n    tuple_collection_2: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...]\n) -> tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes elements of two input tuple collections element-wise, returning a new collection.\n    It validates that corresponding tuples and elements have matching lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple_collection_1) != len(tuple_collection_2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuple collections must have the same number of inner tuples.\")\n\n    result_tuple_collection_list = []\n    for inner_tuple_1, inner_tuple_2 in zip(tuple_collection_1, tuple_collection_2):\n        if len(inner_tuple_1) != len(inner_tuple_2):\n            raise ValueError(\"Corresponding inner tuples must have the same number of elements.\")\n\n        new_inner_tuple_list = []\n        for element_1, element_2 in zip(inner_tuple_1, inner_tuple_2):\n            new_inner_tuple_list.append(max(element_1, element_2))\n        result_tuple_collection_list.append(tuple(new_inner_tuple_list))\n\n    return tuple(result_tuple_collection_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits an input list into 'n' sublists, distributing elements based on their original index modulo 'n'.\n    Each element with original index 'j' goes into the sublist at index 'j % n'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Split factor 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    sublists = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for j, element in enumerate(input_list):\n        i = j % n\n        sublists[i].append(element)\n\n    return sublists"}
