{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef _kadane(arr: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray within a single given array using Kadane's algorithm.\n    Handles cases with all negative numbers by returning the largest single element.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far = float('-inf')\n    current_max = 0\n\n    for x in arr:\n        current_max += x\n        if current_max > max_so_far:\n            max_so_far = current_max\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n            \n    # If all numbers are negative, the above logic would return 0 (if initialized current_max to 0).\n    # To correctly handle all negative numbers, we need to consider the largest single element.\n    # A more robust Kadane's handles this implicitly by starting current_max with the first element.\n    # The current implementation (resetting current_max to 0) works if max_so_far is initialized carefully\n    # or if we account for the all-negative case.\n    # Here, a simple way is to check if max_so_far is still 0 after all elements.\n    # However, the standard robust Kadane:\n    max_so_far_robust = arr[0]\n    current_max_robust = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        current_max_robust = max(arr[i], current_max_robust + arr[i])\n        max_so_far_robust = max(max_so_far_robust, current_max_robust)\n    return max_so_far_robust\n\n\ndef _max_prefix_sum(arr: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of any prefix of the given array.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    max_p_sum = float('-inf')\n    for x in arr:\n        current_sum += x\n        if current_sum > max_p_sum:\n            max_p_sum = current_sum\n    return max_p_sum\n\n\ndef _max_suffix_sum(arr: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of any suffix of the given array.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    max_s_sum = float('-inf')\n    for i in range(len(arr) - 1, -1, -1):\n        current_sum += arr[i]\n        if current_sum > max_s_sum:\n            max_s_sum = current_sum\n    return max_s_sum\n\n\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: List[int], n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k == 1:\n        return _kadane(arr)\n\n    max_sum_single_pass = _kadane(arr)\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n    max_p_sum = _max_prefix_sum(arr)\n    max_s_sum = _max_suffix_sum(arr)\n\n    # Initialize result with the max sum found within a single array repetition\n    result = max_sum_single_pass\n\n    # Consider subarrays spanning two repetitions (suffix of first + prefix of second)\n    result = max(result, max_s_sum + max_p_sum)\n\n    # If the total sum of the array is positive, including k-2 full arrays can be beneficial\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        max_sum_k_times = max_s_sum + (k - 2) * total_sum + max_p_sum\n        result = max(result, max_sum_k_times)\n\n    return result"}
