{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits of each number in a list and returns their aggregated sum.\n    This function uses a helper to calculate the digit sum for individual numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _calculate_digit_sum(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the sum of individual digits for a single non-negative integer.\n        \"\"\"\n        digit_sum = 0\n        # Convert number to string to easily iterate over digits.\n        # This handles 0 correctly and negative numbers if they were allowed (but spec says non-negative).\n        for digit_char in str(number):\n            digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n        return digit_sum\n\n    total_aggregated_sum = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        total_aggregated_sum += _calculate_digit_sum(number)\n    return total_aggregated_sum"}
