{"task_id": "Mbpp/414", "solution": "def overlapping(sequence1: 'Sequence', sequence2: 'Sequence') -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if any value in sequence1 exists in sequence2.\n\n    Args:\n        sequence1: The first sequence (e.g., list, tuple).\n        sequence2: The second sequence (e.g., list, tuple).\n\n    Returns:\n        True if any common value is found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sequence1 or not sequence2:\n        return False\n\n    if len(sequence1) <= len(sequence2):\n        set1 = set(sequence1)\n        for item in sequence2:\n            if item in set1:\n                return True\n    else:\n        set2 = set(sequence2)\n        for item in sequence1:\n            if item in set2:\n                return True\n    return False"}
