{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n\n    Args:\n        arr: A list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array must contain at least two integers.\")\n\n    arr.sort()\n\n    # Product of the two largest numbers\n    product1 = arr[-1] * arr[-2]\n    pair1 = (arr[-2], arr[-1])\n\n    # Product of the two smallest numbers (can be two negative numbers)\n    product2 = arr[0] * arr[1]\n    pair2 = (arr[0], arr[1])\n\n    if product1 >= product2:\n        return pair1\n    else:\n        return pair2"}
