{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers in ascending order using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Modifies the input list in-place and returns the sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n // 2  # Start with a large gap, then reduce it.\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2  # Reduce the gap for the next pass.\n    return arr"}
