{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "def sumofFactors(number_value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of even factors for a given positive integer.\n    It leverages the Number and Factor domain classes for this calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    class Factor:\n        \"\"\"Encapsulates a single factor value and determines its parity.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, value: int):\n            self.value = value\n\n        def is_even(self) -> bool:\n            \"\"\"Returns True if the factor's value is even.\"\"\"\n            return self.value % 2 == 0\n\n    class Number:\n        \"\"\"Manages the input number, finds its factors, filters even factors, and calculates their sum.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, value: int):\n            self.value = value\n\n        def get_factors(self) -> list[Factor]:\n            \"\"\"Returns a list of Factor objects for the number.\"\"\"\n            factors = []\n            for i in range(1, int(self.value**0.5) + 1):\n                if self.value % i == 0:\n                    factors.append(Factor(i))\n                    if i * i != self.value:\n                        factors.append(Factor(self.value // i))\n            return factors\n\n        def get_even_factors(self) -> list[Factor]:\n            \"\"\"Returns a list of Factor objects that are even.\"\"\"\n            all_factors = self.get_factors()\n            return [factor for factor in all_factors if factor.is_even()]\n\n        def calculate_sum_of_even_factors(self) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Calculates and returns the sum of all even factors.\"\"\"\n            even_factors = self.get_even_factors()\n            return sum(factor.value for factor in even_factors)\n\n    number_entity = Number(number_value)\n    return number_entity.calculate_sum_of_even_factors()"}
