{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(numbers: list) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum product of a contiguous subarray.\n\n    This function iterates through the array, tracking the maximum and minimum products ending at the current position.\n    It updates the overall maximum product found to handle both positive and negative number multiplications.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0  # Or handle as per specific empty array requirement, 0 for products\n\n    max_so_far = numbers[0]\n    min_so_far = numbers[0]\n    result = numbers[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(numbers)):\n        num = numbers[i]\n\n        # Store max_so_far to calculate min_so_far correctly if it was updated\n        temp_max_so_far = max_so_far\n\n        max_so_far = max(num, max_so_far * num, min_so_far * num)\n        min_so_far = min(num, temp_max_so_far * num, min_so_far * num)\n\n        result = max(result, max_so_far)\n\n    return result"}
