{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "def max_product(arr: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an increasing subsequence of the input array.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i] stores the maximum product of an increasing subsequence ending with arr[i].\n    dp = list(arr)\n\n    # Initialize overall max_product to handle single-element subsequences.\n    max_overall_product = max(arr)\n\n    for i in range(len(arr)):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                candidate_product = dp[j] * arr[i]\n                if candidate_product > dp[i]:\n                    dp[i] = candidate_product\n\n        # Update the overall maximum product.\n        if dp[i] > max_overall_product:\n            max_overall_product = dp[i]\n\n    return max_overall_product"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def tuple_intersection(list1: list[tuple], list2: list[tuple]) -> set[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the intersection of two lists of tuples, irrespective of element order within tuples.\"\"\"\n\n    def _normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"Converts a tuple to a canonical form by sorting its elements.\"\"\"\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n\n    normalized_l1_set = {_normalize_tuple(t) for t in list1}\n    intersection_result = set()\n\n    for t2 in list2:\n        normalized_t2 = _normalize_tuple(t2)\n        if normalized_t2 in normalized_l1_set:\n            intersection_result.add(normalized_t2)\n\n    return intersection_result"}
