{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "def two_unique_nums(numbers_list: list) -> list:\n    # Count the occurrences of each number in the input list.\n    counts = {}\n    for num in numbers_list:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    # Build a new list containing numbers that appear exactly once, preserving their original order.\n    result = []\n    for num in numbers_list:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n    return result"}
