{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(arr1: list[int], arr2: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth smallest element from two given sorted arrays using a merge-like approach.\n    Assumes k is valid (1 <= k <= total_elements).\n    \"\"\"\n    len1 = len(arr1)\n    len2 = len(arr2)\n    ptr1 = 0\n    ptr2 = 0\n    \n    current_kth = -1 # Placeholder, will be updated in the loop\n\n    # Iterate k times to find the kth smallest element\n    for _ in range(k):\n        # Case 1: All elements in arr1 have been processed\n        if ptr1 == len1:\n            current_kth = arr2[ptr2]\n            ptr2 += 1\n        # Case 2: All elements in arr2 have been processed\n        elif ptr2 == len2:\n            current_kth = arr1[ptr1]\n            ptr1 += 1\n        # Case 3: Compare current elements from both arrays\n        elif arr1[ptr1] <= arr2[ptr2]:\n            current_kth = arr1[ptr1]\n            ptr1 += 1\n        else: # arr2[ptr2] < arr1[ptr1]\n            current_kth = arr2[ptr2]\n            ptr2 += 1\n            \n    return current_kth"}
