{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of positions, returning a new list.\n    Handles empty lists and rotations greater than or equal to list size.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective number of positions to rotate (BR4)\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n\n    # Perform the rotation by splitting and concatenating (BR1, BR5)\n    # The last 'effective_positions' elements move to the front.\n    return input_list[n - effective_positions:] + input_list[:n - effective_positions]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def divisible_by_digits(startnum, endnum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range where every number is divisible by every digit it contains.\n    Helper functions are used for digit extraction and divisibility checks.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _get_digits(number):\n        \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from a given integer.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        temp_num = abs(number)\n        while temp_num > 0:\n            digits.append(temp_num % 10)\n            temp_num //= 10\n        return digits[::-1]\n\n    def _is_number_divisible_by_its_non_zero_digits(number):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is divisible by all its non-zero digits.\"\"\"\n        digits = _get_digits(number)\n        for digit in digits:\n            if digit == 0:\n                continue\n            if number % digit != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    result_list = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_number_divisible_by_its_non_zero_digits(num):\n            result_list.append(num)\n    return result_list"}
