{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "def max_sum_list(list_of_lists: list[list[int]]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the sublist from a list of lists whose sum of elements is the highest.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _calculate_sum(sublist: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements in a single list.\"\"\"\n        return sum(sublist)\n\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return []\n\n    max_sum = float('-inf')\n    max_sum_sublist = []\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_sum = _calculate_sum(sublist)\n        if current_sum > max_sum:\n            max_sum = current_sum\n            max_sum_sublist = sublist\n\n    # If all sublists are empty, or the input was like [[],[]], max_sum will still be -inf\n    # and max_sum_sublist will be the initial [].\n    # This check ensures we return [] in those specific cases.\n    if max_sum == float('-inf') and not any(list_of_lists):\n         return []\n\n    return max_sum_sublist"}
